            <ArticleTitle>Acute superior mesenteric artery occlusion complicated by basilar artery occlusion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>500-503</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.radcr.2017.04.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute mesenteric ischemia is a rare cause of abdominal pain with a very high mortality rate. Vague presentation and often misleading clinical findings make the diagnosis elusive. Here, a unique case of complete superior mesenteric artery occlusion further complicated by basilar artery occlusion is illustrated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
